abstract: >
  MIDAS (Multi-unit Ice Deposits Analysis and Simulation) is a 3D thermo-mechanical
  ice-sheet modelling framework developed as an extension of the Ice-sheet and Sea-level
  System Model (ISSM). It enables simulation of stratified ice masses composed of
  alternating H₂O and CO₂ ice units, capturing rheological, thermal, and dynamic
  contrasts relevant to the Massive CO₂ Ice Deposits (MCID) at Mars’ South Pole.
  MIDAS incorporates temperature-dependent rheologies, density, and thermal conductivity
  variations to study the formation, stability, and flow dynamics of exotic planetary
  ices.
